{"raw": {"https://apply.appone.com/job/6ac8d41fe522c76b590bbef7": {"title": "Biology 121 Adjunct Professor", "description": "Biology 121 Adjunct Professor. Temporary. Mars Hill, NC. Posted 2026-10-09T11:46:39.8636256Z. Biology 121 Adjunct Professor Mars Hill University Biology 121 Adjunct Professor Share this page We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, marketing, and to improve your experience and our services. We use third party technologies that may access your information. By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use. For more information, see our Privacy Policy . Continue Connection lost, sorry about that... Something went wrong while accessing this data. Please check your internet connection and retry. Retrying... Retry failed, please try again. Please try again later Open jobs Biology 121 Adjunct Professor Apply Job description Mars Hill University seeks an energetic, engaging adjunct instructor to bring biology to life for science majors during the Spring 2027 semester. The instructor will teach lectures and labs for Introduction to Cells &amp; Genetics (BIO121), part of a 2-course introductory sequence for biology, zoology, and related majors, helping students explore the living world through relevant examples, meaningful discussions, and hands-on investigations. The course is currently scheduled to be taught with lectures MWF at 1 pm, and labs Monday 2-5 pm and possibly Tuesday 8- 11 am, so the ideal candidate would be available to teach at those times.\n\nWe are looking for someone passionate about biology, enthusiastic in the classroom, and eager to help students see how science connects to the world around them. A Ph.D. in biology or a closely related field is preferred; however, we also strongly encourage candidates with a master\u2019s degree and college-level teaching experience to apply. To be considered, please submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae or r\u00e9sum\u00e9, and contact information for two professional references. Mars Hill, NC Onsite Temporary About Mars Hill University Mars Hill University is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in the mountains of western North Carolina. Founded in 1856 by Baptist families of the region, it is the oldest institution of higher learning in western North Carolina on its original site.\n\nMars Hill University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin, sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity), age, disability, religion, veteran\u2019s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Terms of use I understand and acknowledge that by clicking \"submit,\" the information provided will be shared with both the company to which I am applying (\"Client\") and Paychex, Inc. and its affiliates (\"Paychex\"), Client's authorized third-party service provider. Paychex is not responsible for Client's compliance with applicable federal, state, and local statutes, regulations, or ordinances. Client is solely responsible for complying with all applicable laws. Paychex does not represent or warrant that materials provided comply with applicable federal and state laws and regulations, nor whether any Client use of a particular functionality of the service is appropriate or otherwise lawful. Any and all materials provided as part of this service are not intended as legal advice. If you have a specific problem, issue, or need for legal or financial advice, the services of a relevant professional should be sought to address the particular situation. Paychex expressly disclaims any liability associated with a Client's use of this service. I further understand that Paychex may use a third-party vendor to perform some of the service. I warrant that I possess the full power and authority to provide this authorization and submit this information, and I acknowledge that I am responsible for the security of all usernames, passwords, or other login credentials used to access the service. OK Powered by Privacy Policy \u00b7 Terms of Use \u00b7 \u00a9 2008\u20132026 PAYCHEX All rights reserved. Job posting loaded"}, "https://apply.appone.com/job/6aa7e1dd3861abcc0a59f6ea": {"title": "Director of Financial Aid", "description": "Director of Financial Aid. Full Time. Mars Hill, NC. Posted 2026-09-22T12:32:00.764136Z. Director of Financial Aid Mars Hill University Director of Financial Aid Share this page We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, marketing, and to improve your experience and our services. We use third party technologies that may access your information. By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use. For more information, see our Privacy Policy . Continue Connection lost, sorry about that... Something went wrong while accessing this data. Please check your internet connection and retry. Retrying... Retry failed, please try again. Please try again later Open jobs Director of Financial Aid Apply Job description The Director of Financial Aid is primarily responsible for directing and coordinating all activities related to administering on-campus financial aid programs, as well as overseeing and operating the financial aid office. \nA Bachelor\u2019s Degree and 3-5 years of experience at Assistant and/or Director level in Financial Aid is required.  The Director must have detailed knowledge of federal, state, NCAA, and institutional regulations pertaining to Financial Aid and have experience with an automated Financial Aid system.  The Director must be able to manage and supervise office staff.  The Director must meet demanding deadlines and work under the stress inherent in this busy college office.  Must possess incisive analytical abilities.  Excellent oral and written communication skills are required.  Knowledge of financial aid leveraging and basic enrollment principles desired.  Exceptional interpersonal and counseling skills, including the ability to gain cooperation through discussion, consensus building, and persuasion.  This position requires some night and/or weekend work as well as some travel.\n\nESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS:   \n\u2022\tComply with federal, state, NCAA, donor, and institutional regulations in the awarding of funds to students attending Mars Hill University.\t\n\u2022\tInterpret federal, state, and NCAA regulations and implement campus procedures that adhere to them.\n\u2022\tPrepare the annual application for campus-based funds (FISAP).\n\u2022\tConduct annual student budget preparation.\n\u2022\tDetermine and fulfill information needs from Admissions, the Registrar, the Business Office, the Athletic Department, etc., for use in the award process.\n\u2022\tPrepare other administrative reports required for the programs.\nSuch as the North Carolina Legislative Tuition Grant and the North Carolina Contractual Scholarship Fund.\n\u2022\tDevelop awarding guidelines and packaging procedures.\n\u2022\tDevelop and maintain the FAO Policies and Procedures Manual.\n\u2022\tDevelop all financial aid forms and brochures used by the FAO and assist in the preparation of standard publications used by the campus.\n\u2022\tAssist in the design and implementation of an automated financial aid system, including Department of Education software and guarantee agency software.\n\u2022\tRepresent the campus to outside constituencies, such as the Student Aid Group, NC Association of Independent Colleges and Universities, etc.\n\u2022\tCounsel individual students who require special handling or insight to avoid further communication through higher-level campus channels.\n\u2022\tProvide information to the Business Office on changes in federal regulations.\n\u2022\tProvide input to financial aid and enrollment proposals, policies, and procedures being developed.\n\u2022\tManage the office operational budget and approve expenditures accordingly.\n\u2022\tCoordinate any special activities related to informing students and parents about the financial aid program at MHU.\n\u2022\tConduct presentations when necessary.\n\u2022\tComplete various surveys related to student financial aid.\n\u2022\tAttend State and Federal training sessions as required.\n\u2022\tServe on various campus committees.\n\u2022\tPerform other duties or special projects. Mars Hill, NC Onsite Full Time About Mars Hill University Mars Hill University is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in the mountains of western North Carolina. Founded in 1856 by Baptist families of the region, it is the oldest institution of higher learning in western North Carolina on its original site.\n\nMars Hill University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin, sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity), age, disability, religion, veteran\u2019s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Terms of use I understand and acknowledge that by clicking \"submit,\" the information provided will be shared with both the company to which I am applying (\"Client\") and Paychex, Inc. and its affiliates (\"Paychex\"), Client's authorized third-party service provider. Paychex is not responsible for Client's compliance with applicable federal, state, and local statutes, regulations, or ordinances. Client is solely responsible for complying with all applicable laws. Paychex does not represent or warrant that materials provided comply with applicable federal and state laws and regulations, nor whether any Client use of a particular functionality of the service is appropriate or otherwise lawful. Any and all materials provided as part of this service are not intended as legal advice. If you have a specific problem, issue, or need for legal or financial advice, the services of a relevant professional should be sought to address the particular situation. Paychex expressly disclaims any liability associated with a Client's use of this service. I further understand that Paychex may use a third-party vendor to perform some of the service. I warrant that I possess the full power and authority to provide this authorization and submit this information, and I acknowledge that I am responsible for the security of all usernames, passwords, or other login credentials used to access the service. OK Powered by Privacy Policy \u00b7 Terms of Use \u00b7 \u00a9 2008\u20132026 PAYCHEX All rights reserved. Job posting loaded"}, "https://apply.appone.com/job/6aac2ab92548b6339d6bf4c1": {"title": "Mailroom Supervisor", "description": "Mailroom Supervisor. Part Time. Mars Hill, NC. Posted 2026-09-17T18:00:26.0850355Z. Mailroom Supervisor Mars Hill University Mailroom Supervisor Share this page We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, marketing, and to improve your experience and our services. We use third party technologies that may access your information. By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use. For more information, see our Privacy Policy . Continue Connection lost, sorry about that... Something went wrong while accessing this data. Please check your internet connection and retry. Retrying... Retry failed, please try again. Please try again later Open jobs Mailroom Supervisor Apply Job description Through dynamic, innovative approaches, Student Life is a robust program that gives students opportunities for meaningful engagement and transformation in the co-curricular context. The mailroom supervisor is responsible for efficiently and promptly distributing mail for the college community; maintaining accurate accounts for postage billing; handling supply purchases; and supervising post office staff, including student employees.  The Mailroom Supervisor works under the supervision of the AVP/DOS.\nEssential Responsibilities:  \n\u2022\tHave a daily set schedule (M-F) that does not change unless necessary\n\u2022\tProcess all outgoing mail (sort, weigh, affix correct postage, certify, and insure)\n\u2022\tAssist administrative offices with questions regarding large mailings\n\u2022\tDistribute inter-office mail. This includes all mail and packages, handouts, and flyers for faculty, staff, and students\n\u2022\tKeep records of departmental postage and make monthly reports to the business office\n\u2022\tSupervise the student workers\n\u2022\tKnow and understand the package locker system and scan all packages in a timely manner (day of delivery)\n\u2022\tCollect and file all student paper mail efficiently \n\u2022\tAssume responsibility for distributing information regarding official closings due to holidays and school breaks\n\u2022\tResponsible for maintaining postal machine finances and addressing mechanical issues\n\u2022\tCommunicate with Facilities to ensure proper working box keys and box lock maintenance\n\u2022\tCommunicate with postage delivery services, town post office, and paid postal contract\n\u2022\tResponsible for Student Workers; hiring, training, hours, schedule, timesheets, and work contract\n\u2022\tResponsible for working with Campus Security for daily post office mail pickup\n\u2022\tEnsure outgoing mail is delivered to the Post Office\n\nQualifications:  High school graduate or equivalent; college degree preferred\n\u2022\tTwo years of secretarial and administrative support experience strongly preferred\n\u2022\tDemonstrated experience with Microsoft Office, spreadsheet software, email, and PowerPoint preferred\n\u2022\tKnowledge of United States Postal Service mailing regulations\n\u2022\tWell organized, able to set priorities and deal with matters in a tactful and highly confidential manner\n\u2022\tCapable of working independently and with students in a supervisory role\n\u2022\tAbility to work under pressure and deal with deadlines (essential)\n\u2022\tComfortable with multi-tasking; flexible with fluid situations and effective with changing priorities\n\u2022\tPrevious customer-service oriented work, including the ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with students, parents, alumni, faculty and staff\n\u2022\tSolid communication skills required\n\u2022\tStrong interpersonal skills (emotionally intelligent)\n\u2022\tStrong commitment to the values of diversity and human compassion Mars Hill, NC Onsite Part Time About Mars Hill University Mars Hill University is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in the mountains of western North Carolina. Founded in 1856 by Baptist families of the region, it is the oldest institution of higher learning in western North Carolina on its original site.\n\nMars Hill University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin, sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity), age, disability, religion, veteran\u2019s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Terms of use I understand and acknowledge that by clicking \"submit,\" the information provided will be shared with both the company to which I am applying (\"Client\") and Paychex, Inc. and its affiliates (\"Paychex\"), Client's authorized third-party service provider. Paychex is not responsible for Client's compliance with applicable federal, state, and local statutes, regulations, or ordinances. Client is solely responsible for complying with all applicable laws. Paychex does not represent or warrant that materials provided comply with applicable federal and state laws and regulations, nor whether any Client use of a particular functionality of the service is appropriate or otherwise lawful. Any and all materials provided as part of this service are not intended as legal advice. If you have a specific problem, issue, or need for legal or financial advice, the services of a relevant professional should be sought to address the particular situation. Paychex expressly disclaims any liability associated with a Client's use of this service. I further understand that Paychex may use a third-party vendor to perform some of the service. I warrant that I possess the full power and authority to provide this authorization and submit this information, and I acknowledge that I am responsible for the security of all usernames, passwords, or other login credentials used to access the service. OK Powered by Privacy Policy \u00b7 Terms of Use \u00b7 \u00a9 2008\u20132026 PAYCHEX All rights reserved. Job posting loaded"}, "https://apply.appone.com/job/6a74e3932c4184d6c0b37709": {"title": "Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach", "description": "Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach. Full Time. Mars Hill, NC. Posted 2026-08-06T19:56:27.193394Z. Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach Mars Hill University Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach Share this page We use cookies and other technologies to support site functionality, analytics, preferences, marketing, and to improve your experience and our services. We use third party technologies that may access your information. By continuing to use our site, you expressly consent to such use. For more information, see our Privacy Policy . Continue Connection lost, sorry about that... Something went wrong while accessing this data. Please check your internet connection and retry. Retrying... Retry failed, please try again. Please try again later Open jobs Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach Apply Job description The Assistant Coach assists with all aspects of the Women\u2019s Lacrosse program.\nMars Hill competes at the NCAA Division II level and is a member of the South Atlantic Conference. The successful candidate must have a strong commitment to the academic success of the student-athletes in the program that leads to graduation through a positive collegiate experience. The Assistant Coach reports to the Head Coach and the Director of Athletics.\n\nEssential Responsibilities:\n\u2022\tAssist with essential daily tasks that are vital in running a successful NCAA Division II Athletic program\n\u2022\tOn and off-campus recruiting of quality prospective student-athletes\n\u2022\tAttend and/or plan fundraising activities\n\u2022\tAssist with practice planning and implementation\n\u2022\tGame day responsibilities as directed by Head Coach\n\u2022\tOrganize and participate in community engagement activities\n\u2022\tMonitor academic status and progress of student-athletes\n\u2022\tFilm review and preparation of scouting reports as directed by Head Coach\n\u2022\tField work and maintenance of softball facility as directed by Head Coach\n\u2022\tAssist in developing and monitoring an effective strength and conditioning program\n\u2022\tAssist Head Coach with social media accounts and positively promote the Women\u2019s Lacrosse program\n\u2022\tAdministrative responsibilities related to scheduling, organizing travel, and general office duties\n\u2022\tEffective communication with current student-athletes as well as prospective student-athletes\n\u2022\tAdhere to MHU, SAC and NCAA rules and regulations\n\u2022\tOther duties as assigned by Head Coach and/or Director of Athletics\n\nQualifications:\t\nApplicants should have at least a bachelor\u2019s degree with a successful coaching background in Women\u2019s Lacrosse. Strong communication, organizational skills and a demonstrated ability to produce and manage Women\u2019s Lacrosse programs are important.\n\nIn accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), MHU provides reasonable accommodation to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities unless the accommodation would impose an undue hardship on the organization or would change the essential functions of the job. Requests for reasonable accommodation should be directed to Human Resources (see below).\n\nMHU is committed to hiring faculty and staff who fully support MHU\u2019s mission.  In accordance with federal law and U.S. Department of Agriculture policy, this institution is prohibited from discriminating on the basis of race color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex, familial status, sexual orientation, and reprisal.\n\nTo file a complaint with Mars Hill University, contact:\nJennie Matthews\nOffice of Human Resources\nBox 6664\nMars Hill University\nMars Hill, NC 28754\n828 689-1197\n828 689-1256 Fax\njmatthews@mhu.edu\nTo file a complaint of discrimination, write to:\nUSDA, Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights\nOffice of the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights\n1400 Independence Avenue, S.W., Stop 9410\nWashington DC 20250-9410\nOr call toll-free at (866) 632-9992 (English) or (800) 877-8339 (TDD) or (866) 377-8642\n(English Federal- relay) or (800) 845-6136\n(Spanish Federal-relay).\nUSDA is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Mars Hill, NC Onsite Full Time About Mars Hill University Mars Hill University is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in the mountains of western North Carolina. Founded in 1856 by Baptist families of the region, it is the oldest institution of higher learning in western North Carolina on its original site.\n\nMars Hill University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, or national origin, sex (including sexual orientation, gender identity), age, disability, religion, veteran\u2019s status, or any other protected basis under applicable law in the recruitment and admission of students, the recruitment and employment of faculty and staff, or the operation of any of its programs and activities. Terms of use I understand and acknowledge that by clicking \"submit,\" the information provided will be shared with both the company to which I am applyin